    "body": "> What do you intend with the PSi4 driver? The method of getting the data back across processes was the QMolecule which had no dependence on any else in Qiskit. At present its marked deprecated - depending on where you want to go with PSi4 driver maybe an easy solution is to have a copy (non-deprecated) of the QMolecule in with PSI4 driver so it uses that 'private' copy internally to the driver.\r\n\r\nThe PSi4 driver is awaiting a refactoring as part of the Epic #166 (same like some other drivers). It depends on the HDF5 driver whose refactoring needs further discussion (#302). I intentionally want to keep using the deprecated QMolecule here. There is no benefit in copying the the QMolecule to an internal class.\r\nI can add an improved warning message to the driver stating that it will undergo a pending refactoring in Qiskit Nature 0.3.0 if you like. Same with the other drivers.",
